{"body":{"text":["The foundation is built, and the field is kept in seven stores, all in strata. The engine, written anew, reads and commits over them, every expression in them now written as uses, and the interface draws on it at `/`; the earlier engine and its format are gone, the first integration, the location, joins the page to the browser's address and history, and every other program is still to be built."]},"id":"1M87MMGTJ5A8000","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A component is a holon, and says in it only what it says, its `input`, and its body where it is data. Its holon names its code on each surface, under `realized`, on the web the path of its file in `components/web/`, whose default export draws it; the chassis, in `chassis/web/`, finds every component in one read and loads what each names (`chassis/web/realized.ts`), and the build builds what the field names, so no table binds code to components: \"the chassis should naturally find the component because they are already in the available field … and the components code is linked to the holons of the components\" (22/7). The path stands until code is read through git, as the author set (22/9). The components themselves are a store of their own, `components/.glass`, standing on glass: \"do you mean components are declared in the root .glass? That doesn't make sense. Definitely not\" (22/37). The chassis names no component: whoever starts it gives it how code is loaded and, by route, the ones it draws for its own cases, the one that chooses where several could draw a value, the fallback, and Problem, as OpenLight's chassis mounted components of its own (21/39); it stands apart from the components it draws, since a local chassis will come beside the web's: \"we know we're going to want local chassis anyway\" (20/19). *The chassis broken away, the author's, 20/17 and 20/19; where the code lies the session's (20/18); built.* Some components, as the reader and search, are defined wholly in the field, as layout and data (15/19). *Components as holons, settled 2026-11-11.* A component declares its `input` as a function does, a list of types matched by type (18/27), and is applied by a use, which names it and gives it what it is to show; mount folds into use, \"I'm fine with the dropping mount until we feel the need of it again\" (18/71). *Settled, 18/93; built. The chassis given a component for its own case of a problem, the author's, 21/39; built. Each component naming its code, the author's (22/7), a path for now (22/9); the components a store of their own at his word (22/43); built.*"]},"id":"1M87MMGTJ5A8001","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The chassis's look holds its tokens, which every component draws with and a site tunes, and what the chassis makes itself, a drawing's host and a line where even Problem could not draw, in `chassis/web/look/`. A link is made in one place, `components/web/link.ts`, by the param q the page reads, over the location's way of making an address; the chassis makes none: \"Having some kind of link thing in the chassis naturally doesn't make sense\" (22/11). No component reads the address: an answer says what was asked by its steps, as the pills say them, and a list keeps how it was shown by what it holds. The breadcrumb is one read of `wholes`, its names in one round after, and the start one of `roots`, functions written in the language. *The session's, at the author's word to clean what it could before he reviews (20/21); built.*"]},"id":"1M87MMGTJ5A8002","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The page hosts and decides little: it starts the engine and each store in a worker of its own, and the location on its own thread, mounts them, and draws its root read, Reader given what the address asks. Which components show, and how they are laid out, are read from the field. It is `site/page.ts`, served at `/`, and gives the chassis how component code is loaded; the language as glass ships it, its types and the functions everything applies found by route, is `language/shipped.ts`, and the interface is no module of the code but this program, the page running a chassis with its components on the engine (20/18). What the chassis draws nothing of is the page's: the inspector, on right-click, `site/inspector.tsx`, and the bar showing the page busy while the chassis waits on reads, `site/busy.ts`."]},"id":"1M87MMGTJ5A8003","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The query is no store of the page's: it is what the browser's address asks, its param q, read as `get(@location:params, \"q\")` from the location, the integration holding the address and the history (Meeting the world). There is one source of truth, and nothing is kept in step with it: \"There's only one source of truth in the field, and that's how it is. That's why we have reverse functions\" (22/11). What is typed goes back on Enter, through the way back, to that param, and the location writes it to the address as a step in the history; a pill taken out the same; a link followed is the browser's own, taken by the location without loading a page, so the engine keeps running. As one types, only completion is offered. The page names its stores in its own code, as the author leaned: \"the site that we want built will define its stores in the sites. ts i would think\" (11/7), and took at 18/17: \"on point three: ok\". *Settled, 18/17. The query the location's, the author's (22/11, 22/13); built.*"]},"id":"1M87MMGTJ5A8004","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The page's root, Reader given what the address asks, is a line of its own code, so the top of the page's holarchy stands in no store; only the layouts it reaches, Reader's and Search's, are held uses in glass (19/17, 19/18). A store of the site's own, web based and with persistence, perhaps begun from the site's code and needing no dotfile in the repository, is to come once components can be changed. *Leaning, 19/19: \"one that i guess is a web based one, with persistance\".*"]},"id":"1M87MMGTJ5A8005","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The reader is what the page draws: a component of data laying search above the answer, both given what the address asks, search parsing it itself so the way back ends in `print` and lands in the location's param. *Text and not a use, the session's, at the author's word \"use common sense\" (18/95, 18/96); built.* Search lays the text's steps as pills beside an input that continues them: typing `| something` adds a step, anything else asks anew, and Backspace in the empty input takes the last step back to edit. Pressing a pill's × proposes the steps without it, back through `each`, `chain` and `print` into the address, which keeps names. The answer follows on Enter, not as one types."]},"id":"1M87MMGTJ5A8006","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A site is a page that starts glass upon stores it names in its own code. This project's site is built from every store the repository holds, read as it stands, nothing converted; `bun run serve` serves each store live from its folder, and the page at any path holding nothing, and every page starts its own engine over what it is served, so a page opened after a commit made by the author's tools reads it. The site store, `site.json` and the attachments are gone, as the author took (18/17). Each module is built at its own path in the repository, and the page names what it starts, its looks and its stores from the site's root, so it opens at any path, a single-page app at the author's word, \"Sure turn on SPA for our app\" (22/23), the location taking every path of its origin."]},"id":"1M87MMGTJ5A8007","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The site is published as the repository's pages on GitHub, built from main by its workflow at every push, on the author's own domain (19/25). The build copies each store and prepares its index, copying a store only once its heads hold still and failing rather than publish one missing a blob its heads name (19/30); GitHub's cache may keep a head some 10 minutes after a deploy, naming blobs the deploy no longer has; that the published site might instead read the repository itself, as git serves it in plain files, is the git integration's to show (19/21, 19/24). The build writes the page again as `404.html`, which GitHub's pages serve at any path they hold nothing at, as single-page apps there are made (22/21, 22/22); such a path answers 404, unseen by a person: the path Deep paths answered 404."]},"id":"1M87MMGTJ5A8008","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The string buffer was built before the interface, as the author asked: \"let's build buffers before building the interface\" (18/15). It is a store in memory, in any runtime, keeping the store's contract: an act replaces what it touches and moves the head, and nothing earlier is kept. It keeps the names of its heads, so a change's `at` is checked as any store's, but not what they held, so a strict change made from before the present is refused, since it cannot tell what moved; one not strict is taken. A string is one holon whose body holds its text. The page's query was one, held in step with the address, until the author held there is one source of truth (22/11): the query is now the address itself, through the location."]},"id":"1M87MMGTJ5A8009","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The field this repository holds is seven stores, each a strata store, each found by the `.glass/` beside what it is about. Glass, at the repository's root, holds glass's own types grouped as wholes, store, language, prose and interface, with the functions it ships. Components, in `components/`, holds the components, taken out of glass into a store of their own, whole by itself and standing on glass (22/37, 22/43). Location, in `integrations/location/`, holds what the location is, served by the location itself while it runs (Meeting the world). Wiki, in `wiki/`, holds Knowledge, the threads and the old wiki as it stood, and keeps the root id of the store once called main. Author, in `author/`, holds the author's words, As it was said, the sessions, the measures and the statistics, and paper and paper-readings stand beneath it. *Proposed, 18/104, the author answering it point by point at 18/105; built.* *The components' store the author's, 22/43; cut by one act written to each store, as the engine cannot yet move a holon between stores, every id kept (22/44): the thread Residence follows holding.*"]},"id":"1M87MMGTJ5A800A","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Glass stays one store, its things namespaced within it as wholes, so each may later be loaded and depended on alone: \"It actually has its own structure, so maybe that's fine because we're namespacing inside the store anyway\" (18/105). The store holding Knowledge is wiki: \"Maybe we want to call it wiki\" (18/105). Measures and statistics stand with what they relate to: \"they should probably be stored with where they are\" (18/105); the cut put the measures with the author, since every one points at a session. *Leaning, 18/105.* The components were the first so taken away (22/44)."]},"id":"1M87MMGTJ5A800B","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["One way is built, the location, the browser's address and history both ways, given beneath. The reading of git went with the earlier engine it was built on, and git comes back first; every other way below is still to be."]},"id":"1M87MMGTJ5A800C","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The location is the first integration built: the browser's address and its history, projected into the field and written back, a program serving the engine. \"I would expect it to project the properties of the history stack and the location in the field in a first class manner\" (22/13). It is `integrations/location/`, three holons beneath its root: `address`, where the page is, its origin, path and hash; `params`, what the address asks, each param a key of its body, and so of no type, since a mould names its keys; and `history`, its entries, each an address, and `at`, the index of the one shown, or, where the browser has no Navigation API, only how many there are. *Asked by the author, 22/13; its shape the session's (22/14, 22/16); built.*"]},"id":"1M87MMGTJ5A800D","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The browser is the one source of truth, and nothing is kept in step with it (22/11): a read reads it, and the store moves whenever the browser does, by a link followed, back and forward, or a change it took. A change is written back as the way back gives it, through `get`'s reverse, \"get() then has a reverse so changes can propagate\" (22/15): params and the hash a step in the history, the path one within its scope, history's `at` a move through it. The entries are the browser's alone, and the origin is never written, since leading to another site would take the page, and all that would hear, with it (22/18). Its scope is given as it starts: `page`, its own path, or `origin`, every path of the origin, as a single-page app routes them, a link to any taken without loading a page: \"having SPA control is a good requirement\" (22/19). The site runs it in `origin` (22/23). It follows the browser only from its first subscriber to its last, so an engine unmounting it lets it go (22/20). *Built, 22/16 to 22/24.*"]},"id":"1M87MMGTJ5A800E","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["What it is it ships in its own store, the `.glass` beside its code: its root, standing on glass; the types `address` and `history`; and the three holons. Running, it serves that same store, the same holons under the same ids and addresses, their bodies the browser's; not running, strata serves it as kept, so whatever depends on it reads it alike: \"could the running integration serve the same holons, under the same address, unifying and simplifying from one point of view\" (22/37). It is started given only its scope, finding its store where it lies, by `browser.ts` in a page and `machine.ts` on a machine, departing from a store being handed its storage (12/135) for sovereignty: \"autonomy is part of our core value, sovereignty, standing whole by itself\" (22/31). *The author's, 22/31 and 22/37; built, 22/44.* In a page it finds its store where the site publishes it, which the author holds cannot stay: \"it can't be hard-bound to some URL, this is the discussion to take as we progress with git integration\" (22/45). *Open: the thread Where an integration finds its own store.* One location runs over its `.glass` at a time; several are the path Many running locations."]},"id":"1M87MMGTJ5A800F","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
